Error [E0105]: Case `.Bad` of `CheckAgeError` is created with two different payloads
  --> inferred_failure_case_payload_conflict.jet:5:30
    |
  5 |     if age < 0 -> return Err(.Bad(age))
    |                              ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Every `Err(.Bad(…))` in `check_age` adds to the one type `CheckAgeError`, so each case has one payload
 Fix: Give the two failures different case names, or pass the same payload types to `.Bad`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0105

Error [E0108]: The payload of `CheckAgeError.Bad` holds String (text), but this value is Int (a whole number)
  --> inferred_failure_case_payload_conflict.jet:5:35
    |
  5 |     if age < 0 -> return Err(.Bad(age))
    |                                   ^^^
 Why: A variant payload keeps the type its enum declaration gives it
 Fix: Put the value in text with interpolation: "{x}"
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0108
